HYMNs and Other Eigenvalues for GR(2, 2)

As shown by Eq. (4.47), there are 64 possible GR(2, 2) valise and raised adinkras. The eigenvalues of
L1(m, w)R1(µ, w), L2(m, w)R1(µ, w), R1(µ, w)L1(m, w), R1(µ, w)L2(m, w), R2(µ, w)L1(m, w), and
R2(µ, w)L2(m, w) deﬁne eigenvalue equivalence classes of GR(2, 2) adinkras. We ﬁnd

• all sixteen valise GR(2, 2) adinkras give the same eigenvalues:
L1(m, w)R1(µ, w) : {1 , 1}; L2(m, w)R1(µ, w) : {i , −i};
R1(µ, w)L1(m, w) : {1 , 1};
R1(µ, w)L2(m, w) : {i , −i}; R2(µ, w)L1(m, w) : {i , −i};
R2(µ, w)L2(m, w) : {1 , 1}

• all GR(2, 2) adinkras with one boson raised give the same eigenvalues:
L1(m, w)R1(µ, w) : {1 , ρ};
L2(m, w)R1(µ, w) : {i√ρ , −i√ρ}; R1(µ, w)L1(m, w) : {1 , ρ};
R1(µ, w)L2(m, w) : {i√ρ , −i√ρ}; R2(µ, w)L1(m, w) : {i√ρ , −i√ρ}; R2(µ, w)L2(m, w) : {1 , ρ}

